iker who survived the  crash returns periodically to taunt her  curves should have made a bigger splash  than it did but it got lost in early  2016 and went straight to streaming  however the theaters lost was Netflix's  game so catch it on the streaming  service before it disappears round the  bend the Lazarus effect released in 2015  this movie about a serum that can bring  people back to life was almost  completely overlooked on sheer star  power alone  the Lazarus effect is virtually  unmatched as an under-the-radar horror  movie with Olivia Wilde mark Duplass  donald glover sarah Bolger and Evan  Peters all working their magic to  elevate a less than inspired concept  into legitimately scream worthy  territory and while it's true that the  script could be tighter don't believe  the lack of hype on this one the Lazarus  effect is a far better movie than its  low rating on Rotten Tomatoes would  suggest 1922 Netflix definitely knew  what it was doing when it snagged this  little story for a screen adaptation  based on a novella from Stephen King's  full dark no stars anthology 1922 stars  Thomas Jane as Wilfred James a farmer  living in rural Nebraska during the  period leading up to the Great  Depression money troubles and marital  conflict lead wilfred to some very dark  places and it just goes to show that  sometimes getting away with a crime is  much worse than getting caught that  murdered my wife to keep my home the  only way I was leaving it now would be  in change like many of Stephen King's  best works this is a character-driven  horror and strong performances make a  stand out particularly from Jane who  immerses himself in the role so  thoroughly that it's hard to believe  this same miserable hate you and Yoko is  the same cosmopolitan pretty boy from  the sweetest thing you're never gonna  find anyone better than my brother Eyrie  is the greatest and I am scared not just  just look at them chicks freak on this  guy creeped in 2014 filmmaker Patrick  Brice set out to answer the question  what's the worst thing that could happen  from meeting someone on Craigslist  without spoiling anything let's just say  the answer is something really bad  that's what a videographer discovers  when he goes to the home of Joseph  played by Mark Duplass who also co-wrote  and produced a movie for what's supposed  to be a documentary project what starts  out as the ordinary weirdness of  internet strangers becomes something  much more disturbing that's peach fuzz  that's it's just peach fuzz say hello  the result is a movie that more than  lives up to its title  Gerald's game with so many blockbusters  on the big screen in 2017 you might have  missed some of the smaller adaptations  of Stephen King's works including this  one based on the 1992 novel of the same  name  Gerald's game centers on a woman who  ends up trapped hadn't cuffed to the bed  at her lake house after her husband has  a heart attack as she struggles to find  a way to escape she's visited by a  series of entities some real some  imagined and some that seem to straddle  the line between this world and the next  [Music]  one of Netflix's original feature films  Gerald's game was eagerly anticipated by  hardcore King fans but didn't get the  kind of widespread attention merited by  its creativity in star power despite the  obvious challenges of holding down an  entire two-hour film on her own actress  carla Gugino keeps it riveting making  this the finest horror movie set almost  entirely on a bed since well maybe ever  unless you count bet at the day a dark  song this Irish independent horror movie  flew under the radar when it was  released in 2017 but the handful of film  buffs who did see it were impressed and  with good reason a dark song centers on  a grieving mother who hires an occultist  to guide her through a complex  months-long right at a remote home in  the Welsh countryside despite a teensy  budget and a very green director at a  tone a dark song boasts